🪵 Search existing log summaries in the running viewer. The default window is the last hour; output uses aligned columns unless --json is set.

USAGE
  otel-desktop-viewer logs [flags]

EXAMPLES
  otel-desktop-viewer logs
  otel-desktop-viewer logs --service checkout --since 30m
  otel-desktop-viewer logs --start 2026-10-02T08:00:00Z --end 2026-10-02T09:00:00Z --json

FLAGS
      --end string        Inclusive RFC3339 end time (nanoseconds supported)
      --endpoint string   Running viewer HTTP endpoint (default "http://localhost:8000")
      --json              Emit the summary response as JSON instead of columns
      --limit int         Maximum summaries to return (default 25)
      --service string    Only summaries for this service
      --since duration    Relative lookback window (for example 30m, 6h, or 24h) (default 1h0m0s)
      --start string      Inclusive RFC3339 start time (nanoseconds supported)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  -h, --help   Help for this command
